# 9. Gradients

Use subtle gradients.

### Light mode example

```text
linear-gradient(
  135deg,
  #F9DDE8,
  #DDEEFF,
  #FFE4C7
)
```

### Dark mode example

```text
linear-gradient(
  135deg,
  #17151D,
  #39264D,
  #0E0D12
)
```

Gradients should appear mainly in:

* hero sections,
* backgrounds,
* cards,
* AI sections,
* profile headers.

Never use gradients behind dense clinical text.

---

# 10. Glassmorphism

Glass effects should be used selectively.

Example:

```css
background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
```

Dark mode:

```css
background: rgba(30, 27, 38, 0.65);
backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
```

Use glassmorphism for:

* navigation
* floating cards
* profile headers
* appointment cards
* AI interaction panels
* modal overlays

Do not use heavy glass effects on every element.

---

