# 111. UX Quality Checklist

Every major screen must pass:

### Clarity

Can a first-time user understand the page within 3 seconds?

### Action

Is the primary action obvious?

### Accessibility

Can the patient use it without relying entirely on vision or typing?

### Feedback

Does every action produce visible feedback?

### Recovery

Can the user recover from failure?

### Responsiveness

Does it work on mobile and desktop?

### Motion

Does animation improve understanding rather than distract?

