# 114. Final User Experience

The patient experience should feel like:

```text
Open Quantum Care
       ↓
Create Profile
       ↓
Tell us what you're feeling
       ↓
Speak or tap
       ↓
AI asks only relevant questions
       ↓
Review your health summary
       ↓
Upload medical records
       ↓
Find hospital
       ↓
Book appointment
       ↓
Receive QR
       ↓
Arrive at hospital
       ↓
Check in later through kiosk
       ↓
Doctor receives structured history
```

The UI should make this journey feel like **one continuous experience**, rather than a collection of unrelated forms.

The visual layer is there to reduce cognitive load, not to win a CSS competition. The original problem specifically requires the system to remain usable for elderly, low-literacy and varied-language users, so the aesthetic system must always remain subordinate to comprehension and accessibility.
